// TEST: Comm Over Virtual Range Operands Licenses Nothing
// Compaction keys on an IDENTITY GROUP -- the SAME array occupying the commuting
// operand slots (formalism.md 11.2/12.4; rawAxisGroups.mergesWith.acrossArray
// demands sameArrayIdentity). A virtual `range<...>` operand never materializes,
// so every one gets a fresh AIDLiteral and no identity group can EVER form: the
// comm group merges no axes and the clause is dropped. `dense` below emits C++
// byte-identical to the same kernel with no `where` clause -- dense
// Array<double, 2> over {3,3}, inner bound `__i1 < 3`, all nine cells written.
//
// This is symmetry/004 and /014's class (comm without array identity gets
// nothing), but those stay SILENT on purpose: a real array can be its own
// identity partner at another call site (symmetry/003 is that call site), so the
// clause there is unused, not dead. A range operand is incapable of it at EVERY
// call site, so here the refusal is stated rather than taken silently -- BL4017.
// Warning, not error: the program is correct, just not the one that was asked
// for. Nothing is disproved (cf. BL4013) and nothing unsound is licensed (cf.
// BL4016); the clause is simply inert.
// WARN: BL4017
let A: Array<Float64 like Idx<3>> = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let dense = method_for(range<Idx<3>>, range<Idx<3>>) <@> lambda(i, j) where comm(i, j) -> A(i) * A(j) |> compute
// EXPECT: dense = [[1.0, 2.0, 3.0], [2.0, 4.0, 6.0], [3.0, 6.0, 9.0]]

// The alternative the diagnostic points at: symmetry declared in the INDEX TYPE.
// This one really does allocate the triangular pool (`r_symm`) and iterate only
// canonical cells (`__i1 < 3 - __i0`) -- six stored cells against `dense`'s nine,
// which is what the dropped clause was asking for. It carries no `where` clause
// at all, so it doubles as the negative control: BL4017 keys on an inert CLAUSE,
// not on `range<...>` operands.
let compact = method_for(range<SymIdx<2, 3>>) <@> lambda(i, j) -> A(i) * A(j) |> compute
// EXPECT: compact = [[1.0, 2.0, 3.0], [2.0, 4.0], [3.0]]
